# Code owners for brubru.
#
# What this does and does NOT do, so nobody mistakes it for a gate:
#
# It does NOT stop a direct push to main. Nothing in CODEOWNERS blocks a push, and
# this repo ships by pushing straight to main. CODEOWNERS only bites on PULL
# REQUESTS: the owner is automatically requested for review, and a ruleset option
# ("require review from Code Owners") can then make that review mandatory before a
# merge. No such ruleset exists here yet, deliberately.
#
# So why have it: brubru is a PUBLIC repository. Anyone on GitHub can open a pull
# request against it, including one that edits a workflow file. A workflow runs
# code, so an edit to .github/ is the highest-value change a stranger could
# propose. This file guarantees those pull requests land in Victor's review queue
# rather than sitting unnoticed.
#
# Last pattern to match a file wins, so order matters: general first, specific last.

# Everything, by default.
*                       @victorsole

# Workflows and repo automation: these execute code in CI with repository access.
/.github/               @victorsole
/.github/workflows/     @victorsole

# Secrets-adjacent and deploy-adjacent configuration.
/backend/core/config.py @victorsole
/backend/Dockerfile     @victorsole
/.gitignore             @victorsole
